// A policy with a genuine SYNTAX error: the predicate is missing its `::<kind>` segment, and the
// field is missing its `input.` group prefix.
//
// Both are what AWS's temporal-policies article prints for its mutual-exclusion policy, and the
// reference implementation rejects it:
//
//     × unexpected token `{`, expected comparison operator
//
// It is here because our own parser reads a SUBSET, so it has two ways to fail and one message for
// both. On this file it says `expected '::', got '{'` -- which reads like a limitation of Anchor,
// and is not: the policy is broken. Telling those apart is what `--syntax` and the refusal path
// exist for, and this fixture is the case that distinguishes them.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_sell",
    resource
)
unless {
    context.input.profit < 0 && temporal {
        formerly within 24h (
            AgentCore::Action::"execute_buy"{
                stock_symbol: context.input.stock_symbol}
        )
    }
};
